1
00:00:02,135 --> 00:00:03,967
NARRATOR: <i>Previously on</i> Gotham:

2
00:00:04,137 --> 00:00:07,369
- You need to leave Ms. Kringle alone.
- I get it now.

3
00:00:07,541 --> 00:00:09,806
You got a thing for my girl.

4
00:00:10,844 --> 00:00:12,073
[GRUNTS]

5
00:00:12,713 --> 00:00:13,942
Oh, dear.

6
00:00:14,114 --> 00:00:15,673
[LAUGHS]

7
00:00:16,016 --> 00:00:17,382
Who sent you?

8
00:00:17,551 --> 00:00:20,453
You want me to tell
Bunderslaw that you're onto him?

9
00:00:20,621 --> 00:00:21,782
[SCREAMS]

10
00:00:23,857 --> 00:00:25,826
- I'm Bruce Wayne.
- Sid Bunderslaw.

11
00:00:27,928 --> 00:00:32,366
The people of Gotham deserve to know that
there is a serial killer in their midst.

12
00:00:32,533 --> 00:00:34,001
<i>I'm coming after you.</i>

13
00:00:34,167 --> 00:00:38,002
He murders the loved ones of
any cop who investigates him.

14
00:00:38,171 --> 00:00:40,106
Care to dance?

15
00:01:00,527 --> 00:01:02,587
Morning. How'd you sleep?

16
00:01:02,763 --> 00:01:04,925
The hour we slept?

17
00:01:05,098 --> 00:01:06,726
Great.

18
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:09,369
You hungry? I have quiche.

19
00:01:09,536 --> 00:01:10,765
No, thanks.

20
00:01:11,204 --> 00:01:12,399
At least have some coffee.

21
00:01:12,573 --> 00:01:15,873
Let me tell you about the
day I have planned for us.

22
00:01:16,043 --> 00:01:19,104
- I think I'm just gonna get out of here.
- Wait.

23
00:01:21,715 --> 00:01:24,207
We had fun last night, right?

24
00:01:29,222 --> 00:01:30,246
Stay.

25
00:01:33,093 --> 00:01:35,961
- Listen, you don't have to do this.
- Do what?

26
00:01:36,129 --> 00:01:39,759
Last night at the ball,
you talked a good game.

27
00:01:39,933 --> 00:01:42,562
But let's not pretend this
is more than what it is.

28
00:01:42,736 --> 00:01:45,228
Barbara, I'm not
pretending with you.

29
00:01:45,405 --> 00:01:48,739
I want you to stay with me.

30
00:01:49,743 --> 00:01:51,177
I don't think so.

31
00:01:51,411 --> 00:01:52,879
Wait, wait, wait.

32
00:01:53,647 --> 00:01:55,309
Let go.

33
00:01:56,083 --> 00:01:57,517
Look...

34
00:01:58,652 --> 00:02:02,817
I was pretending with you.

35
00:02:03,957 --> 00:02:06,586
But not in the way you think.

36
00:02:08,996 --> 00:02:10,589
[SIGHS]

37
00:02:13,900 --> 00:02:16,096
The night we met...

38
00:02:17,537 --> 00:02:19,335
I was going to kill you.

39
00:02:22,476 --> 00:02:23,637
That's not funny.

40
00:02:23,810 --> 00:02:24,937
But then...

41
00:02:26,179 --> 00:02:29,047
I saw something in you.

42
00:02:29,216 --> 00:02:31,344
Barbara, I saw...

43
00:02:31,518 --> 00:02:34,647
the real you.

44
00:02:38,025 --> 00:02:41,860
You're the woman that I
have been searching for.

45
00:02:45,732 --> 00:02:47,564
You're lying.

46
00:02:51,004 --> 00:02:53,564
I'm gonna let you go now.

47
00:02:54,675 --> 00:02:57,235
And you're going to sit down...

48
00:02:57,444 --> 00:02:59,879
and have breakfast with me.

49
00:03:06,386 --> 00:03:07,877
[GRUNTS]

50
00:03:15,328 --> 00:03:16,352
No!

51
00:03:18,198 --> 00:03:20,394
So we'll do it the hard way.

52
00:03:30,010 --> 00:03:32,707
- Hey. How are you doing?
- I've been better.

53
00:03:32,879 --> 00:03:36,475
- Have you seen Harvey?
- No. Any word on Barbara?

54
00:03:37,117 --> 00:03:40,747
They haven't found her body yet,
so there's a chance she's still alive.

55
00:03:40,921 --> 00:03:43,948
- When's the last time you slept?
- I don't know.

56
00:03:44,124 --> 00:03:45,148
Last time you ate?

57
00:03:45,325 --> 00:03:45,984
I don't know.

58
00:03:46,008 --> 00:03:48,193
I know better than to
try to get you to sleep.

59
00:03:48,361 --> 00:03:50,626
- But you really should eat.
- I'm not hungry.

60
00:03:50,797 --> 00:03:52,766
Jim.

61
00:03:52,933 --> 00:03:54,367
It's not your fault.

62
00:03:56,703 --> 00:04:01,437
I did this. I pressed Loeb, he sent
the Ogre after me, and I didn't stop.

63
00:04:01,608 --> 00:04:06,444
It's bad enough I knowingly put you in
danger. I didn't even think of Barbara.

64
00:04:06,613 --> 00:04:08,946
- You were doing your job.
- But I should've known.

65
00:04:09,116 --> 00:04:11,642
How? You weren't together.

66
00:04:11,818 --> 00:04:14,378
Do you blame yourself
for falling out of love?

67
00:04:14,554 --> 00:04:18,150
Lee, it's my responsibility. There's
nothing you can say that changes that.

68
00:04:18,325 --> 00:04:21,090
Whatever happens
to Barbara, it's on me.

69
00:04:22,229 --> 00:04:24,221
- I understand. BULLOCK: Jimbo.

70
00:04:24,965 --> 00:04:26,558
Meet Jake the JV pimp.

71
00:04:26,733 --> 00:04:29,066
He's been bragging that
he knows who the Ogre is.

72
00:04:29,236 --> 00:04:32,900
I keep telling you, man, you
been lied to. I don't know nothing.

73
00:04:33,073 --> 00:04:35,099
- Yeah, we'll see about that.
- Unh.

74
00:05:14,648 --> 00:05:16,207
Okey-doke.

75
00:05:16,383 --> 00:05:20,184
No body, no crime.
No body, no crime.

76
00:05:21,454 --> 00:05:24,652
Nope. Never seen him before.

77
00:05:26,393 --> 00:05:29,386
We think this is a serial
killer called the Ogre.

78
00:05:30,163 --> 00:05:32,462
He's kidnapped a woman,
and he's gonna kill her...

79
00:05:32,632 --> 00:05:33,998
unless we find him first.

80
00:05:34,167 --> 00:05:35,191
Bummer.

81
00:05:35,368 --> 00:05:36,836
Just so you understand...

82
00:05:37,003 --> 00:05:40,701
the lady in question is a
real good friend of ours.

83
00:05:40,874 --> 00:05:46,142
Supposing, for the sake of
argument, I did see him before.

84
00:05:46,313 --> 00:05:47,542
What's she worth?

85
00:05:49,382 --> 00:05:51,351
What's she worth?

86
00:05:51,518 --> 00:05:53,180
Yeah, you know...

87
00:05:54,020 --> 00:05:55,886
if you had to assign
a dollar amount.

88
00:05:58,692 --> 00:06:03,494
Harvey, I'm about to violate departmental
policy on interrogation techniques.

89
00:06:04,698 --> 00:06:08,692
I think I saw some doughnuts
outside with my name all over them.

90
00:06:10,070 --> 00:06:12,733
Hey, now. Calm yourself.
There's no need to...

91
00:06:15,909 --> 00:06:18,845
Jake worked as a barman at
a brothel called the Foxglove.

92
00:06:19,012 --> 00:06:21,675
Said the Ogre was a regular.
Can't give us a location.

93
00:06:21,848 --> 00:06:23,874
Because they never
use the same place twice.

94
00:06:24,050 --> 00:06:25,712
- You know it?
- Not personally.

95
00:06:25,886 --> 00:06:29,015
The Foxglove is very
high-class, very extreme.

96
00:06:29,189 --> 00:06:31,215
You gotta know someone
who knows someone.

97
00:06:31,391 --> 00:06:34,520
- I might know someone.
- You talking Penguin?

98
00:06:34,694 --> 00:06:36,890
Get any deeper with that
clown, he will own you.

99
00:06:37,063 --> 00:06:39,161
I don't have a choice.
The Ogre has Barbara.

100
00:06:39,185 --> 00:06:40,431
Let me shake a few trees.

101
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:43,229
Take the time, grab
some Z's. You're burnt.

102
00:06:44,738 --> 00:06:46,400
The first one was the hardest.

103
00:06:46,573 --> 00:06:50,806
But it wasn't her fault.
She just wasn't the one.

104
00:06:50,977 --> 00:06:52,946
I also couldn't let her go.

105
00:06:53,113 --> 00:06:57,574
Still, it strengthened my resolve to
never stop till I found my soul mate...

106
00:06:57,751 --> 00:07:00,550
the person I could
share everything with.

107
00:07:02,322 --> 00:07:05,918
I think that person is you,
Barbara. But I need your help.

108
00:07:06,660 --> 00:07:08,094
So...

109
00:07:08,828 --> 00:07:11,423
let's begin again, shall we?

110
00:07:15,702 --> 00:07:16,726
[MUFFLED SCREAM]

111
00:07:24,444 --> 00:07:30,076
This just, um, came for you
by messenger, Master Bruce.

112
00:07:32,719 --> 00:07:34,278
Thank you.

113
00:07:37,791 --> 00:07:41,455
Right, well, I ought to be off.

114
00:07:41,661 --> 00:07:42,959
Do you want company?

115
00:07:45,198 --> 00:07:48,794
To identify Reggie? No, I
don't think so. Best done alone.

116
00:07:50,470 --> 00:07:52,598
I'm sorry, Alfred.

117
00:07:52,772 --> 00:07:55,708
- I know he was your friend.
- Just doesn't make any sense.

118
00:07:56,576 --> 00:07:58,545
Reggie topping
himself like that.

119
00:07:58,712 --> 00:08:02,376
You said he fell out of a window. He
might have been drinking, lost his balance.

120
00:08:02,549 --> 00:08:03,573
[SCOFFS]

121
00:08:03,750 --> 00:08:05,981
That Reggie was a legend.

122
00:08:06,553 --> 00:08:09,387
He could be blind drunk
and walk a tightrope.

123
00:08:10,957 --> 00:08:13,620
It doesn't matter what
he was like in the end.

124
00:08:14,828 --> 00:08:17,627
I wanna see he gets
a proper send-off.

125
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:22,796
I'll see you this evening, sir.

126
00:08:48,428 --> 00:08:51,159
LIDIA: What? Your boss
doesn't trust his partners?

127
00:08:51,331 --> 00:08:55,098
It's called due diligence. He just
wants me to look the place over.

128
00:08:55,268 --> 00:08:56,930
So look.

129
00:08:57,103 --> 00:09:00,301
I got a gravy going.
Special party today.

130
00:09:00,473 --> 00:09:02,305
Don't let me keep you.

131
00:09:02,675 --> 00:09:04,473
Piece of work.

132
00:09:15,989 --> 00:09:20,324
BUTCH: <i>I put the pistol under the
bar, machine gun behind the juke.</i>

133
00:09:22,028 --> 00:09:24,998
All Connor and his guy
gotta do is get to them.

134
00:09:25,498 --> 00:09:27,160
The day is finally here.

135
00:09:28,301 --> 00:09:29,769
Maroni...

136
00:09:30,870 --> 00:09:34,466
Jim. So lovely to see you.

137
00:09:34,641 --> 00:09:37,475
To what do I owe this
wonderful surprise?

138
00:09:38,478 --> 00:09:42,176
I need to know where the
Foxglove is. And I need an invitation.

139
00:09:42,348 --> 00:09:44,214
[LAUGHING]

140
00:09:44,384 --> 00:09:46,319
Well, someone's in a mood.

141
00:09:46,986 --> 00:09:48,648
Can you help me out? Yes or no?

142
00:09:50,223 --> 00:09:54,251
Jim, I do so love our
give-and-take relationship.

143
00:09:54,427 --> 00:09:56,487
But it's starting to
feel a bit one-sided.

144
00:09:57,230 --> 00:10:00,325
Fine. I'll owe you a favor.

145
00:10:00,934 --> 00:10:03,836
- You already do.
- Then I'll owe you another.

146
00:10:05,171 --> 00:10:07,163
Cards on the table?

147
00:10:08,007 --> 00:10:11,444
The Foxglove makes a lot of
money for some important...

148
00:10:11,611 --> 00:10:13,079
[GASPS]

149
00:10:15,748 --> 00:10:20,186
You think you know who
I am, what I'm capable of?

150
00:10:20,353 --> 00:10:22,413
You have no idea.

151
00:10:22,889 --> 00:10:25,859
Today's an important day for me.

152
00:10:26,025 --> 00:10:28,756
So I will accommodate
your request.

153
00:10:29,129 --> 00:10:32,793
But, detective, mark my words...

154
00:10:32,966 --> 00:10:35,731
you owe me a big favor.

155
00:10:36,236 --> 00:10:37,329
[CHUCKLES]

156
00:10:43,243 --> 00:10:45,644
Here we have the Physical
Operations Department.

157
00:10:45,845 --> 00:10:49,407
The Physical Operations Department
handles logistics for the corporation.

158
00:10:49,582 --> 00:10:51,210
Management of our properties...

159
00:10:51,384 --> 00:10:53,717
Excuse me. I need
to use the restroom.

160
00:10:53,887 --> 00:10:57,881
- Of course, Mr. Wayne. It's right here.
- Thank you.

161
00:11:05,865 --> 00:11:07,663
[ALARM WAILING]

162
00:11:11,371 --> 00:11:14,398
The Foxglove is in the old
Klondike Building on Mayflower.

163
00:11:14,574 --> 00:11:17,169
- You score a ticket?
- Yep. But only one.

164
00:11:17,377 --> 00:11:21,178
I figure you go in, pose as a john,
find something to bust them on...

165
00:11:21,381 --> 00:11:23,612
then we squeeze
them till they talk.

166
00:11:23,783 --> 00:11:25,684
Smart move sending me.

167
00:11:25,885 --> 00:11:28,684
You couldn't look more like a
cop if you wore a blue uniform.

168
00:11:28,855 --> 00:11:31,381
You got something to wear?
You're, uh, gonna need to fit in.

169
00:11:31,558 --> 00:11:34,995
Don't worry. Alvarez busted some
guys smuggling Italian suits last week...

170
00:11:35,161 --> 00:11:38,893
and a couple fell in my locker
on their way to the evidence room.

171
00:11:39,065 --> 00:11:40,533
[CHUCKLES]

172
00:11:41,401 --> 00:11:43,927
LENNON: I'm sorry
I left you alone...

173
00:11:44,637 --> 00:11:49,439
but you needed time to think,
to accept that this was real.

174
00:11:49,609 --> 00:11:54,707
This apartment is soundproof,
by the way, so save your lungs.

175
00:12:09,462 --> 00:12:11,897
Look at me. My
hands are shaking.

176
00:12:12,065 --> 00:12:15,365
That's never happened before with
any of the other women I've had here.

177
00:12:15,535 --> 00:12:17,697
You know why that is?

178
00:12:21,708 --> 00:12:24,576
Do you know why that is?

179
00:12:24,744 --> 00:12:26,906
You're a psycho.

180
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:29,015
I don't know what
you're thinking.

181
00:12:32,652 --> 00:12:34,553
It's because...

182
00:12:34,721 --> 00:12:38,385
I always somehow
knew, deep down...

183
00:12:38,558 --> 00:12:40,550
the others weren't the one.

184
00:12:41,561 --> 00:12:43,587
They weren't the one.

185
00:12:47,367 --> 00:12:48,995
I want this to work, Barbara.

186
00:12:55,608 --> 00:12:58,976
You're scared. It's okay.

187
00:13:02,615 --> 00:13:04,641
Jim will find me. Unh!

188
00:13:09,122 --> 00:13:14,288
The only way you're going to make
me angry is if you mention his name.

189
00:13:25,071 --> 00:13:26,699
Drink this.

190
00:13:27,373 --> 00:13:30,036
It's water. You're dehydrated.

191
00:13:39,519 --> 00:13:42,512
Barbara, come here. I
want you to see something.

192
00:13:47,727 --> 00:13:51,289
Barbara, I love you. I love you
like no one has ever loved you.

193
00:13:51,464 --> 00:13:55,231
But if you try to escape, I will
chain you to the ceiling and gut you.

194
00:13:55,401 --> 00:13:58,735
Now come here.

195
00:14:16,422 --> 00:14:17,685
Are those...?

196
00:14:17,857 --> 00:14:21,817
When you're looking for love,
you have to kiss a lot of frogs.

197
00:14:22,462 --> 00:14:26,661
Still, I should be thankful.
They led me to you.

198
00:14:29,469 --> 00:14:31,495
All those women...

199
00:14:32,939 --> 00:14:34,965
they died here?

200
00:14:36,376 --> 00:14:38,277
You killed them...

201
00:14:38,778 --> 00:14:40,269
here?

202
00:14:41,514 --> 00:14:43,107
Yes.

203
00:14:49,355 --> 00:14:50,880
Don't worry.

204
00:14:51,090 --> 00:14:53,525
I'm gonna set you free.

205
00:14:53,693 --> 00:14:56,561
You're the one, Barbara.

206
00:14:56,729 --> 00:14:58,493
You're the one.

207
00:15:01,567 --> 00:15:03,092
[ALARM WAILING]

208
00:15:42,375 --> 00:15:43,934
[ALARM STOPS]

209
00:15:49,348 --> 00:15:51,374
BUNDERSLAW: Hello, Bruce.

210
00:15:52,151 --> 00:15:54,017
I've been expecting you.

211
00:16:01,093 --> 00:16:05,997
Ever since your friend borrowed
my key, I've been expecting you.

212
00:16:06,165 --> 00:16:08,031
Even canceled my trip.

213
00:16:08,601 --> 00:16:10,160
Cookie?

214
00:16:11,204 --> 00:16:12,695
When I was a boy...

215
00:16:12,905 --> 00:16:15,397
I'd always take a cookie
when I had the chance.

216
00:16:18,978 --> 00:16:20,708
You hired a man to kill Alfred.

217
00:16:20,913 --> 00:16:24,315
I hired your guardian's comrade
to find out what you knew.

218
00:16:24,484 --> 00:16:27,545
I never intended harm
to come to anyone.

219
00:16:30,356 --> 00:16:35,852
I told the board you were a special
case, that you'd need the talk early.

220
00:16:36,028 --> 00:16:37,792
The talk.

221
00:16:37,964 --> 00:16:41,059
Bruce, when members of the
Wayne family reach a certain age...

222
00:16:41,234 --> 00:16:43,703
some facts of life and
business are explained...

223
00:16:43,870 --> 00:16:46,362
Wayne Enterprises is
committing serious crimes.

224
00:16:46,539 --> 00:16:48,633
Oh, my, yes.

225
00:16:48,808 --> 00:16:53,746
This is a multinational corporation
operating in hundreds of jurisdictions.

226
00:16:53,946 --> 00:16:57,747
We do our best to subvert
all of them if it means profits.

227
00:16:59,552 --> 00:17:02,386
- So you admit it?
- Just like your father.

228
00:17:02,855 --> 00:17:06,348
He came in with his secret
files demanding justice...

229
00:17:06,526 --> 00:17:07,550
at first.

230
00:17:08,194 --> 00:17:10,356
Then he changed his mind.

231
00:17:10,530 --> 00:17:11,554
You're lying.

232
00:17:11,731 --> 00:17:15,361
Your father came to understand
the reality of this business.

233
00:17:15,535 --> 00:17:18,027
As did his father,
and as will you.

234
00:17:18,204 --> 00:17:20,196
My father was a good man.

235
00:17:20,373 --> 00:17:25,073
You have an opportunity
to live a blessed life.

236
00:17:25,244 --> 00:17:28,703
The life your father and
mother wanted for you.

237
00:17:30,283 --> 00:17:32,548
I beg you to reconsider.

238
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:36,086
Pardon me.

239
00:17:36,255 --> 00:17:37,951
Lucius, come in.

240
00:17:38,124 --> 00:17:41,856
Bruce Wayne, meet one of
our junior executives, Lucius Fox.

241
00:17:42,028 --> 00:17:45,760
There's a public-relations person
desperately searching for this young man.

242
00:17:45,932 --> 00:17:48,128
Then you'd best reunite them.

243
00:17:48,734 --> 00:17:50,225
Bruce.

244
00:17:50,770 --> 00:17:52,705
Don't forget your cookie.

245
00:18:05,818 --> 00:18:07,184
Now...

246
00:18:08,854 --> 00:18:10,656
I'm going to tell you
something, and I'd

247
00:18:10,680 --> 00:18:12,916
appreciate if you kept
your face perfectly still.

248
00:18:13,092 --> 00:18:16,460
There's cameras everywhere. I
know because I put them there.

249
00:18:16,629 --> 00:18:21,067
What I'm about to say must be a
deep secret between you and me.

250
00:18:21,801 --> 00:18:25,465
I knew your father
well. He was good man.

251
00:18:25,638 --> 00:18:27,800
He wasn't the man the
company thought he was.

252
00:18:29,842 --> 00:18:32,311
- I don't understand you.
- Bruce.

253
00:18:33,179 --> 00:18:35,444
Your father was a true stoic.

254
00:18:35,615 --> 00:18:38,847
He kept his best self hidden.

255
00:18:39,418 --> 00:18:41,614
That's all I'll say.

256
00:18:48,361 --> 00:18:49,989
Good luck.

257
00:19:02,041 --> 00:19:03,373
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

258
00:19:03,542 --> 00:19:06,102
KRISTEN: Mr. Nygma?
- Ms. Kring...

259
00:19:06,278 --> 00:19:07,302
Ms. Kringle?

260
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:09,346
Would you open the door, please?

261
00:19:09,515 --> 00:19:11,609
Um, I'm...

262
00:19:12,318 --> 00:19:13,377
One sec.

263
00:19:24,530 --> 00:19:26,726
I need the Hendricks case files.

264
00:19:26,899 --> 00:19:29,334
Um, yes. Hendricks.
Wait right there.

265
00:19:32,538 --> 00:19:35,372
Hendricks, Hendricks, Hendricks.

266
00:19:37,643 --> 00:19:38,838
Hendricks!

267
00:19:39,078 --> 00:19:41,206
Ahh. Oh, my goodness.

268
00:19:42,314 --> 00:19:45,375
- What happened to him?
- Um, ax.

269
00:19:45,551 --> 00:19:47,179
Accidental death.

270
00:19:47,887 --> 00:19:50,482
At a sheet-metal
factory. Industrial saw.

271
00:19:50,656 --> 00:19:52,124
[BUZZES]

272
00:19:52,625 --> 00:19:54,423
Poor man.

273
00:19:54,627 --> 00:19:57,927
I don't... I don't know
how you do this job.

274
00:19:58,130 --> 00:20:00,622
- Death all around you.
- Heh.

275
00:20:00,800 --> 00:20:03,565
Yes. One must have
a sense of humor.

276
00:20:04,570 --> 00:20:07,438
- The file?
- Yes.

277
00:20:12,278 --> 00:20:14,509
Um, Mr. Nygma.

278
00:20:14,680 --> 00:20:18,048
You haven't by chance seen
Tom...? Officer Dougherty?

279
00:20:18,751 --> 00:20:22,381
We were supposed to have
dinner last night, and he didn't show.

280
00:20:22,555 --> 00:20:25,518
No surprise. But I
haven't seen him today.

281
00:20:25,542 --> 00:20:26,542
Me neither.

282
00:20:27,059 --> 00:20:28,527
Oh.

283
00:20:29,295 --> 00:20:31,812
Excuse me. I really
need to get back to work.

284
00:20:31,836 --> 00:20:32,322
Oh, uh.

285
00:20:32,498 --> 00:20:35,297
- Now.
- Okay. Um...

286
00:20:39,271 --> 00:20:41,069
Oh, dear.

287
00:20:42,541 --> 00:20:46,774
You're sure the guns are there?

288
00:20:46,946 --> 00:20:49,108
Butch placed them himself.

289
00:20:49,281 --> 00:20:52,809
Do you remember what to say
to Maroni before you do the deed?

290
00:20:53,419 --> 00:20:55,752
I never saw the point in
telling a man something...

291
00:20:55,921 --> 00:20:58,117
right before you're
gonna whack him.

292
00:20:58,824 --> 00:21:01,623
But you're not the
first to ask for it.

293
00:21:03,295 --> 00:21:05,491
I appreciate you humoring me.

294
00:21:06,298 --> 00:21:09,962
So how'd you know Maroni's
gonna be in this bar on this exact day?

295
00:21:10,703 --> 00:21:13,002
I follow current events.

296
00:21:20,880 --> 00:21:22,815
[CHUCKLES]

297
00:21:27,787 --> 00:21:32,020
There he is. Tommy
freaking Bones.

298
00:21:32,191 --> 00:21:35,320
Nine years up the river, and you
get better-looking, you big animal.

299
00:21:35,494 --> 00:21:37,793
I took care of myself.

300
00:21:38,998 --> 00:21:40,796
I was hoping you'd remember.

301
00:21:40,966 --> 00:21:42,958
- Ha, ha.
- Come over here. Huh?

302
00:21:43,135 --> 00:21:46,105
Listen, you leave the joint,
you come to Lidia's for dinner.

303
00:21:46,272 --> 00:21:47,968
That's tradition. Welcome home.

304
00:21:48,140 --> 00:21:49,938
Lidia. Look who's here.

305
00:21:50,609 --> 00:21:52,737
[ALL LAUGHING]

306
00:21:55,848 --> 00:21:58,374
[DANCE MUSIC
PLAYING ON SPEAKERS]

307
00:22:05,558 --> 00:22:09,723
Welcome to the Foxglove. The
evening's entertainment is about to begin.

308
00:22:09,895 --> 00:22:12,023
Well, I guess I'm just in time.

309
00:22:20,039 --> 00:22:22,304
[PEOPLE SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY]

310
00:23:05,351 --> 00:23:09,220
Ladies and gentlemen,
your attention, please.

311
00:23:09,922 --> 00:23:14,553
I know you have been eagerly
awaiting tonight's main attraction.

312
00:23:14,727 --> 00:23:20,223
So please, let's give a big Foxglove
welcome to Ingrid and Gareth.

313
00:23:20,399 --> 00:23:22,334
[APPLAUSE]

314
00:23:25,404 --> 00:23:27,032
[WHEELS SQUEAKING]

315
00:23:27,206 --> 00:23:28,640
[INGRID MOANS THEN GIGGLES]

316
00:23:28,807 --> 00:23:30,241
[ENGINE WHIRRING]

317
00:23:30,409 --> 00:23:31,502
GARETH: Ow!

318
00:23:31,677 --> 00:23:32,770
Oh, no.

319
00:23:32,945 --> 00:23:34,379
Hell, no.

320
00:23:34,546 --> 00:23:35,673
[PIG SQUEALS]

321
00:23:35,848 --> 00:23:39,250
G.C.P.D.! Nobody move.

322
00:23:39,418 --> 00:23:41,853
Especially you two.

323
00:23:53,766 --> 00:23:55,598
Barbara.

324
00:23:57,903 --> 00:23:59,929
Wake up, Barbara.

325
00:24:00,105 --> 00:24:01,767
Wake up.

326
00:24:07,279 --> 00:24:09,771
Shh, shh. Come here.

327
00:24:11,984 --> 00:24:14,078
Don't cry. Shh. Shh.

328
00:24:15,587 --> 00:24:17,283
Hey.

329
00:24:18,424 --> 00:24:22,293
There's no need to cry, okay?

330
00:24:24,530 --> 00:24:26,863
You're gonna kill me.

331
00:24:27,299 --> 00:24:29,734
- Do you want me to?
- No.

332
00:24:29,902 --> 00:24:33,703
Then tell me who to kill.

333
00:24:36,008 --> 00:24:37,306
What?

334
00:24:39,611 --> 00:24:43,810
You still don't believe I
love you. You think I'm crazy.

335
00:24:44,016 --> 00:24:46,110
That's fine.

336
00:24:46,285 --> 00:24:48,117
I see the truth.

337
00:24:48,287 --> 00:24:50,119
I see your truth.

338
00:24:50,656 --> 00:24:54,787
I see that you've spent your whole
life trying to kill it, but you can't.

339
00:24:54,960 --> 00:24:56,622
It's too strong.

340
00:24:56,795 --> 00:24:59,629
You revealed it to
me the other night.

341
00:24:59,798 --> 00:25:02,825
I wanna set that free.
I wanna set you free.

342
00:25:03,035 --> 00:25:07,973
You think that me making you
murder someone will make me like you?

343
00:25:08,807 --> 00:25:10,275
That's insane.

344
00:25:11,143 --> 00:25:12,509
You say that...

345
00:25:12,678 --> 00:25:15,944
because you don't know
what it is to live without fear.

346
00:25:16,749 --> 00:25:18,650
But you'll learn.

347
00:25:20,119 --> 00:25:24,284
Now tell me who
you want me to kill.

348
00:25:24,456 --> 00:25:31,192
Or though it breaks my heart,
I will take your life right now.

349
00:25:32,765 --> 00:25:34,495
I can't.

350
00:25:36,435 --> 00:25:38,802
I... I can't.

351
00:25:40,039 --> 00:25:41,063
I can't.

352
00:25:42,307 --> 00:25:47,336
Tell me who to kill.

353
00:25:52,518 --> 00:25:54,214
Okay.

354
00:26:00,826 --> 00:26:02,317
You run this place?

355
00:26:03,862 --> 00:26:05,125
I'm looking for this man.

356
00:26:05,297 --> 00:26:08,529
Arrest me if you want to. I
don't talk about my clients.

357
00:26:09,334 --> 00:26:13,203
One call to the <i>Gazette,</i> they'll
send a reporter down here.

358
00:26:13,372 --> 00:26:16,831
I'll perp-walk each and every one of
your clients in front of the cameras.

359
00:26:17,910 --> 00:26:19,139
How's that sound?

360
00:26:20,846 --> 00:26:22,838
Talk to Sally.

361
00:26:26,718 --> 00:26:29,187
You know him? You're sure?

362
00:26:29,855 --> 00:26:31,721
I'm sure.

363
00:26:42,768 --> 00:26:47,035
He said his name was
Jason. He was sweet.

364
00:26:47,206 --> 00:26:50,176
As soon as I got into his car,
he pulled a hood over my head...

365
00:26:50,342 --> 00:26:51,901
and tied my wrists.

366
00:26:52,077 --> 00:26:55,946
He took me to back to his
apartment. That's where he did this.

367
00:26:56,648 --> 00:26:58,139
I don't know why he let me go.

368
00:26:58,550 --> 00:27:00,917
- When was this?
- Almost nine years ago.

369
00:27:01,086 --> 00:27:04,079
About a year before the first
murder. He was working his way up.

370
00:27:04,256 --> 00:27:06,248
Why didn't you go to the police?

371
00:27:06,425 --> 00:27:10,294
I did. I was a hooker. He
was a rich man with no name.

372
00:27:10,462 --> 00:27:13,227
Anything else you can tell us?
Anything about his apartment?

373
00:27:13,398 --> 00:27:15,765
The smallest detail might help.

374
00:27:17,703 --> 00:27:21,196
The elevator opened
right into the apartment.

375
00:27:21,373 --> 00:27:23,933
You can see out into the
city. We were in midtown.

376
00:27:24,877 --> 00:27:28,905
And there was a big neon sign
on the building across the street.

377
00:27:29,081 --> 00:27:33,109
I could only read the
last four letters, O-Y-A-L.

378
00:27:33,552 --> 00:27:34,781
O-Y-A-L.

379
00:27:35,888 --> 00:27:38,050
- Loyal? Royal?
- Royal.

380
00:27:38,223 --> 00:27:41,125
- The Gotham Royal Hotel.
- That's in midtown. Tenth and Gainsly.

381
00:27:41,293 --> 00:27:42,921
Thank you, Sally.

382
00:27:43,095 --> 00:27:46,497
Promise me, when you
find him, don't arrest him.

383
00:27:47,065 --> 00:27:48,089
Kill him.

384
00:27:49,067 --> 00:27:50,729
You got it.

385
00:27:51,503 --> 00:27:55,998
- Making jokes already. He's out two hours.
- Whoa, fellas. Private party.

386
00:27:56,208 --> 00:27:57,904
CONNOR: Just
here to pay respects.

387
00:27:58,644 --> 00:28:00,442
MARONI: Connor
from the wild northeast.

388
00:28:01,513 --> 00:28:03,914
What's that old man
Falcone want now?

389
00:28:04,082 --> 00:28:06,074
Don Falcone sends
me with his respects...

390
00:28:06,251 --> 00:28:09,949
and a small gift for you and
Tommy Bones on this happy day.

391
00:28:10,122 --> 00:28:11,750
Cheech.

392
00:28:12,858 --> 00:28:17,796
- Forgive my suspicious nature.
- Course. Can't be too careful.

393
00:28:18,497 --> 00:28:20,966
Come here. Let me see this.

394
00:28:23,869 --> 00:28:25,565
<i>Madre Di Dios.</i>

395
00:28:25,737 --> 00:28:27,706
My favorite.

396
00:28:27,873 --> 00:28:29,996
Tell Falcone I
appreciate the gesture.

397
00:28:30,020 --> 00:28:32,436
Don Falcone knew it
was a special occasion.

398
00:28:32,611 --> 00:28:35,638
We got time for a drink.
Lidia. Clean glasses, please.

399
00:28:36,248 --> 00:28:40,652
- The gift comes with a message.
- Oh, yeah? What's that?

400
00:28:40,819 --> 00:28:44,153
He wants you to know that it wasn't
easy for him to decide to kill you.

401
00:28:47,259 --> 00:28:48,852
Son of a bitch.

402
00:28:49,494 --> 00:28:51,827
But business is business.

403
00:28:52,030 --> 00:28:54,522
[CLICKING]

404
00:29:01,206 --> 00:29:02,504
You believe it?

405
00:29:02,674 --> 00:29:05,906
You both jammed. If that ain't a
sign from God, I don't know what.

406
00:29:06,078 --> 00:29:07,478
- Please...
- Shut your mouth.

407
00:29:07,646 --> 00:29:10,138
You're gonna take Don
Falcone a message from me.

408
00:29:10,315 --> 00:29:12,784
You're gonna let him
know that you messed up...

409
00:29:12,951 --> 00:29:15,580
and you're gonna let him
know that I'm coming for him.

410
00:29:16,555 --> 00:29:19,320
Of course, you don't need
to be alive to tell him that.

411
00:29:19,491 --> 00:29:21,187
Tommy, do the honors.

412
00:29:21,360 --> 00:29:22,384
Wait...

413
00:29:27,032 --> 00:29:30,127
[SINGING] <i>All you
punks and all you Teds</i>

414
00:29:30,302 --> 00:29:33,363
<i>National Fronts and Natty Dreads</i>

415
00:29:33,538 --> 00:29:36,565
<i>Mods, rockers,
hippies and skinheads</i>

416
00:29:36,742 --> 00:29:38,335
<i>Keep on fighting
'til you're dead</i>

417
00:29:38,510 --> 00:29:41,844
Connor blew it.
Maroni's still alive.

418
00:29:42,014 --> 00:29:43,983
This is flat.

419
00:29:45,117 --> 00:29:46,517
Did you not hear me?

420
00:29:46,685 --> 00:29:49,985
Maroni is still alive.
You gotta get out of town.

421
00:29:50,522 --> 00:29:52,218
And miss all the fun?

422
00:29:53,625 --> 00:29:55,184
You knew.

423
00:29:55,661 --> 00:29:57,687
You set him up.

424
00:29:57,863 --> 00:30:01,265
I took the firing pins out of
the guns before you hid them.

425
00:30:01,433 --> 00:30:04,995
A spin on a trick I
learned from Maroni.

426
00:30:06,271 --> 00:30:09,537
- But you could have had Maroni dead.
- True.

427
00:30:09,708 --> 00:30:12,007
But I still would've been
under Falcone's thumb.

428
00:30:12,177 --> 00:30:13,736
And that...

429
00:30:13,912 --> 00:30:16,040
has grown intolerable.

430
00:30:16,214 --> 00:30:18,376
No, I'd much rather
Maroni be alive...

431
00:30:19,017 --> 00:30:20,451
and out for blood.

432
00:30:28,694 --> 00:30:32,927
Alas, Officer Dougherty, she's
gonna wonder where you went.

433
00:30:34,933 --> 00:30:36,299
Perhaps a letter?

434
00:30:36,468 --> 00:30:40,530
You could say goodbye,
give her some advice.

435
00:30:40,939 --> 00:30:44,808
Something that might lead her to
make better choices in the future, hmm?

436
00:30:57,222 --> 00:30:59,157
[GRUNTING]

437
00:31:23,749 --> 00:31:25,615
BULLOCK: Jim!

438
00:31:28,387 --> 00:31:29,411
Place is empty.

439
00:31:30,422 --> 00:31:32,288
But there's something
you should see.

440
00:31:38,230 --> 00:31:41,029
You see anything that
connects to Barbara?

441
00:31:42,934 --> 00:31:44,266
Maybe she was never here.

442
00:31:44,436 --> 00:31:47,964
No, she was here. I can
still smell her perfume.

443
00:31:49,508 --> 00:31:52,000
Hey. We're gonna find this guy.

444
00:31:52,177 --> 00:31:54,339
But you need to
prepare yourself...

445
00:31:56,047 --> 00:31:58,380
that we might not
be in time to save her.

446
00:31:58,550 --> 00:32:01,315
- That is not an option.
- It's the most likely option.

447
00:32:01,486 --> 00:32:03,079
[PHONE RINGING]

448
00:32:16,501 --> 00:32:17,901
Hello?

449
00:32:18,069 --> 00:32:19,799
LENNON: <i>Detective Gordon.</i>

450
00:32:19,971 --> 00:32:22,167
<i>I assume you're the one
who triggered the alarm.</i>

451
00:32:22,340 --> 00:32:24,741
You son of a bitch.
Where's Barbara?

452
00:32:24,910 --> 00:32:26,572
<i>With me, of course.</i>

453
00:32:26,778 --> 00:32:28,178
If you've hurt her...

454
00:32:28,346 --> 00:32:30,508
<i>She's as safe as milk.</i>

455
00:32:30,682 --> 00:32:34,084
<i>Safer than she ever was
when she was with you.</i>

456
00:32:34,286 --> 00:32:38,018
- What the hell does that mean?
<i>- She doesn't need your protection, Jim.</i>

457
00:32:38,190 --> 00:32:40,682
<i>Fact is, she never did.</i>

458
00:32:40,859 --> 00:32:43,090
<i>- I'll see you around.</i>
- Wait.

459
00:32:46,231 --> 00:32:48,723
- He was driving.
- To Tahiti if he's smart.

460
00:32:48,900 --> 00:32:50,163
There was a noise, right?

461
00:32:50,702 --> 00:32:52,193
A thumping.

462
00:32:52,370 --> 00:32:56,034
- Like he was going over a bridge.
- You know, I heard a horn.

463
00:32:56,208 --> 00:32:59,372
- Like a train horn.
- Okay. So which bridge has a train?

464
00:32:59,544 --> 00:33:01,877
Um... Damn.

465
00:33:02,047 --> 00:33:04,346
Whitecross. But
that's the upstate train.

466
00:33:05,617 --> 00:33:07,017
Upstate?

467
00:33:07,452 --> 00:33:09,580
<i>That's where her parents live.</i>

468
00:33:16,761 --> 00:33:18,753
Barbara, please.

469
00:33:18,930 --> 00:33:20,296
What's happening?

470
00:33:20,465 --> 00:33:23,526
LENNON: What's happening is
your daughter is finally waking up.

471
00:33:26,538 --> 00:33:28,336
Please?

472
00:33:29,608 --> 00:33:31,770
Barbara, we're
doing this for you.

473
00:33:34,779 --> 00:33:36,839
[WOMAN SCREAMS]

474
00:33:54,666 --> 00:33:58,330
[JAZZ MUSIC PLAYING
INDISTINCTLY ON SPEAKERS]

475
00:34:06,845 --> 00:34:10,304
<i>I never meant to hurt you</i>

476
00:34:27,732 --> 00:34:29,462
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

477
00:34:32,237 --> 00:34:33,899
Jim?

478
00:34:35,607 --> 00:34:37,200
Barbara.

479
00:34:38,076 --> 00:34:40,272
What are you doing here?

480
00:34:51,690 --> 00:34:53,158
[GRUNTS]

481
00:35:00,332 --> 00:35:02,426
You're not supposed to be here.

482
00:35:04,970 --> 00:35:06,097
Where is he?

483
00:35:13,311 --> 00:35:14,904
[BOTH GRUNTING]

484
00:35:41,906 --> 00:35:44,034
Drop it. Drop the
knife, or I'll shoot.

485
00:35:45,710 --> 00:35:48,805
Just an ounce of pressure,
and she'll split right open.

486
00:35:48,980 --> 00:35:50,676
I don't want that.
Do you want that?

487
00:35:51,383 --> 00:35:54,581
It's gonna be all right,
Barbara. It's gonna be all right.

488
00:35:55,420 --> 00:35:59,255
If you cared about this woman,
you never would have come after me.

489
00:35:59,424 --> 00:36:02,861
- I love her more than you ever did.
- Drop the knife.

490
00:36:04,162 --> 00:36:06,393
It won't be me
that slits her throat.

491
00:36:06,564 --> 00:36:08,760
Detective, that's gonna be you.

492
00:36:08,933 --> 00:36:12,267
- Drop it.
- Jim, please.

493
00:36:12,437 --> 00:36:14,702
Just leave us alone.

494
00:36:17,709 --> 00:36:19,371
Hey. Jerk-o.

495
00:36:28,520 --> 00:36:31,115
Barbara? Barbara?

496
00:36:35,560 --> 00:36:38,086
- He's dead?
- Yeah. He's dead.

497
00:36:38,263 --> 00:36:39,822
It's gonna be okay.

498
00:36:40,765 --> 00:36:42,961
Look at me. Barbara.

499
00:36:45,236 --> 00:36:46,602
It's gonna be okay.

500
00:36:59,851 --> 00:37:02,150
Alfred, I never asked you...

501
00:37:02,854 --> 00:37:05,221
how was it yesterday,
seeing Reggie?

502
00:37:06,124 --> 00:37:10,585
Not really an experience I'd
care to repeat, Master Bruce.

503
00:37:11,763 --> 00:37:14,562
But then again, the Reggie
I knew died years ago.

504
00:37:18,937 --> 00:37:21,566
Alfred, I haven't
been honest with you.

505
00:37:24,476 --> 00:37:26,570
After you were hurt...

506
00:37:26,745 --> 00:37:29,510
Selina and I went
looking for Reggie.

507
00:37:31,783 --> 00:37:32,807
We found him.

508
00:37:35,653 --> 00:37:37,679
Did you, now?

509
00:37:37,889 --> 00:37:40,449
He didn't jump or fall.

510
00:37:42,494 --> 00:37:43,792
Selina pushed him.

511
00:37:45,296 --> 00:37:47,424
And why did she do that?

512
00:37:48,700 --> 00:37:51,295
Reggie was sent here by a
man named Sid Bunderslaw.

513
00:37:51,936 --> 00:37:54,201
Bunderslaw works
for Wayne Enterprises.

514
00:37:54,405 --> 00:37:55,600
Reggie gave us the name...

515
00:37:55,774 --> 00:37:58,608
but said he was gonna tell
Bunderslaw what we were doing.

516
00:37:59,778 --> 00:38:01,440
I see.

517
00:38:03,148 --> 00:38:04,776
And the rest?

518
00:38:06,417 --> 00:38:07,817
The charity ball?

519
00:38:07,986 --> 00:38:10,148
Presumably to have
access to Mr. Bunderslaw.

520
00:38:11,022 --> 00:38:14,015
Selina stole the
key to his office safe.

521
00:38:14,559 --> 00:38:17,119
I went there
today. It was empty.

522
00:38:18,663 --> 00:38:20,564
But Bunderslaw
was waiting for me.

523
00:38:20,732 --> 00:38:21,893
- What did he do?
- Nothing.

524
00:38:22,066 --> 00:38:23,967
- What did he do?
- Nothing.

525
00:38:26,037 --> 00:38:28,199
But he said that my
father and grandfather...

526
00:38:28,373 --> 00:38:32,538
knew about the illegal things that
the company was doing, and chose...

527
00:38:33,011 --> 00:38:35,344
They chose to stay quiet.

528
00:38:38,349 --> 00:38:39,715
[SIGHS]

529
00:38:41,886 --> 00:38:44,446
Your father was a good man.

530
00:38:45,557 --> 00:38:47,082
I know.

531
00:38:49,661 --> 00:38:52,495
But even good men have secrets.

532
00:38:53,865 --> 00:38:55,356
MAN 1: Good job. MAN 2: Yeah.

533
00:38:55,533 --> 00:38:57,365
MAN 1: Very well
deserved. MAN 3: Well done.

534
00:38:57,535 --> 00:39:00,004
- Man of the hour.
- Please.

535
00:39:01,372 --> 00:39:04,365
MAN 3: Very well. MAN
4: That guy right there.

536
00:39:04,542 --> 00:39:06,511
Congratulations. You're a hero.

537
00:39:06,678 --> 00:39:09,409
It won't last. Tomorrow
they'll go back to hating me.

538
00:39:09,581 --> 00:39:11,072
Well, then I'll remind them.

539
00:39:12,917 --> 00:39:16,854
Yesterday you were trying to
help. I couldn't hear it. I'm sorry.

540
00:39:17,555 --> 00:39:20,081
I would never try
to change you, Jim.

541
00:39:20,258 --> 00:39:22,921
Your sense of mission, it's
part of what I love about you.

542
00:39:23,094 --> 00:39:25,529
I thought it was my
devastating good looks.

543
00:39:25,697 --> 00:39:26,721
That's a joke.

544
00:39:27,532 --> 00:39:29,125
[LAUGHS]

545
00:39:31,035 --> 00:39:32,230
I was scared.

546
00:39:33,838 --> 00:39:35,568
Scared that Barbara
would get hurt...

547
00:39:35,740 --> 00:39:38,904
and you would blame
yourself for protecting me first...

548
00:39:39,077 --> 00:39:41,410
and then whatever
we had would die.

549
00:39:42,280 --> 00:39:45,148
It wasn't heroic.
It was selfish.

550
00:39:50,722 --> 00:39:51,951
Lee, I love you.

551
00:39:53,024 --> 00:39:54,117
Not her.

552
00:39:55,059 --> 00:39:58,154
If I had to do it again,
I'd still protect you first.

553
00:40:04,802 --> 00:40:06,395
What did you do?

554
00:40:06,571 --> 00:40:09,405
Grabbed a knife by the blade.

555
00:40:10,441 --> 00:40:11,841
Of course you did.

556
00:40:12,043 --> 00:40:14,308
- Let me see.
- Agh.

557
00:40:20,251 --> 00:40:21,844
Ms. Kringle?

558
00:40:22,921 --> 00:40:24,355
Are you okay?

559
00:40:26,324 --> 00:40:28,691
I got a letter from
Officer Dougherty.

560
00:40:29,294 --> 00:40:30,922
He left town.

561
00:40:32,297 --> 00:40:33,356
[CLEARS THROAT]

562
00:40:33,531 --> 00:40:35,673
"Don't wait around for
me. Go have some fun,

563
00:40:35,697 --> 00:40:38,060
and maybe I'll give you
a call when I get back."

564
00:40:38,236 --> 00:40:42,173
Blah-blah-blah. Couldn't
even tell me to my face.

565
00:40:42,340 --> 00:40:45,276
I mean, why do I
keep picking creeps?

566
00:40:46,844 --> 00:40:49,871
Sometimes with men, you
need to read between the lines.

567
00:40:50,081 --> 00:40:53,347
Sometimes with
men, you need a drink.

568
00:40:54,152 --> 00:40:56,587
Good day, Mr. Nygma.

569
00:41:01,759 --> 00:41:03,489
Read between the lines.

570
00:41:04,362 --> 00:41:06,126
[LAUGHING]

571
00:42:27,478 --> 00:42:29,913
Everybody listen up.

572
00:42:30,415 --> 00:42:32,444
Just got wind of three
separate attacks on

573
00:42:32,468 --> 00:42:34,716
Falcone businesses in
different parts of town.

574
00:42:34,886 --> 00:42:38,152
Word is it's Maroni.

575
00:42:38,322 --> 00:42:40,839
As of right now, all
leaves are canceled

576
00:42:40,863 --> 00:42:43,659
and all units are
called in for active duty.

577
00:42:43,828 --> 00:42:46,821
We're in a shooting war, people.

578
00:43:12,290 --> 00:43:14,725
[LAUGHING]

579
00:43:57,435 --> 00:43:59,427
[English - US -SDH]
